course: dictionary
lesson: 9133
title: Snailfish in the deep
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some animals live where it is very dark, very cold and squeezed by the weight of the water above them. The snailfish is one of them. Its name gives a clue: it is a fish that is soft and slow, a bit like a snail.
explain: «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies, so the pressure does not crush them.» The words around pressure are the clue. Soft, watery bodies are not crushed, so pressure must be the heavy push of the water. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Snailfish live in deep trenches, thousands of metres down in the ocean. Scientists call some of them «hadal snailfish». You may not have seen one, but words like deep-sea and trench tell you where these fish live.
fact: A snailfish is a small, soft, tadpole-shaped fish.
fact: A snailfish has smooth, jelly-like skin and no scales.
fact: Some snailfish live deeper in the ocean than almost any other fish.
fact: «Hadal snailfish» means a snailfish that lives in the deepest ocean trenches.
fact: A snailfish was filmed at over 8,000 metres, one of the deepest fish ever seen.
exercise: What is a snailfish's skin like? | Rough and covered in scales | *Smooth and jelly-like | Hard like a shell | Hairy like a dog
exercise: «A snailfish is a small, soft, tadpole-shaped fish.» What shape is it? | Flat like a leaf | Round like a ball | *Tadpole-shaped | Square like a box
exercise: Where do some snailfish live? | In shallow rock pools | On top of mountains | *In deep trenches, thousands of metres down | In hot desert sand
test: «Some snailfish live in deep trenches.» What does trench mean? | Tall hills on land | A shallow puddle | A fast river | *A deep ditch in the ocean floor
test: «Snailfish were filmed at over 8,000 metres.» What does metres measure? | Weight | Temperature | *Length or distance | Time
exam: In «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies, so the pressure does not crush them», which clue best helps you guess what pressure means? | It is a long, dry bone | It is a pressure cooker used for food | It is a bright light in the dark | *The bodies are soft and watery, so they are not crushed by a heavy push
